### Banking Transaction System - sample requests
### Open in IntelliJ IDEA or VS Code (REST Client extension) and click "Send Request".

@base = http://localhost:8080/api

### 1. Create a customer
POST {{base}}/customers
Content-Type: application/json

{ "fullName": "Anil Katroth", "email": "anil@example.com", "phone": "9652336856" }

### 2. Open a savings account (note the accountNumber in the response, e.g. 100000000001)
POST {{base}}/accounts
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerId": 1, "accountType": "SAVINGS" }

### 3. Open a second account (e.g. 100000000002)
POST {{base}}/accounts
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customerId": 1, "accountType": "CURRENT" }

### 4. Deposit
POST {{base}}/accounts/100000000001/deposit
Content-Type: application/json

{ "amount": 5000.00, "description": "Salary" }

### 5. Transfer (send this twice: the second call returns the same result, money moves once)
POST {{base}}/transfers
Content-Type: application/json

{ "fromAccountNumber": "100000000001", "toAccountNumber": "100000000002",
  "amount": 1200.00, "referenceNo": "RENT-OCT-2026", "description": "October rent" }

### 6. Withdraw more than the balance -> 422 Insufficient funds
POST {{base}}/accounts/100000000002/withdraw
Content-Type: application/json

{ "amount": 99999.00 }

### 7. Account details
GET {{base}}/accounts/100000000001

### 8. Statement for a date range
GET {{base}}/accounts/100000000001/statement?from=2026-10-01&to=2026-10-31

### 9. Monthly summary (from the database view)
GET {{base}}/accounts/100000000001/summary

### 10. Look up a transaction by reference
GET {{base}}/transactions/RENT-OCT-2026

### 11. Freeze an account (transfers to/from it are then rejected)
PATCH {{base}}/accounts/100000000002/status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "FROZEN" }

### 12. All accounts of a customer
GET {{base}}/customers/1/accounts
